WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.157
My wife had been watching Fritz try to catch the giant sturgeon.

2
00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:20.016
"The buffalo!" she cried suddenly.

3
00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:24.121
"Harness him to the harpoon rope, and you'll land that fish!"

4
00:00:24.122 --> 00:00:28.906
Jack ran off to fetch Storm, and we soon captured the sturgeon.

5
00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:33.447
When we'd caught as many fish as possible, we began preserving them.

6
00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:39.722
We'd have plenty to eat next winter because our crops were growing well at both Tentholm and Falconhurst.

7
00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:43.169
Our animals were also thriving.

8
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:50.096
In fact, we had so many animals that we built a farm called Woodlands.

9
00:00:50.097 --> 00:00:54.651
One of our new animals was a bull that had been born during the rainy season.

10
00:00:54.652 --> 00:00:58.521
"Who'll take charge of this fine animal?" I asked my sons.

11
00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:03.253
"I'd rather train Knips," said Ernest as the monkey climbed on his shoulder.

12
00:01:03.254 --> 00:01:07.022
"I'm too busy with my buffalo and jackal," said Jack.

13
00:01:07.023 --> 00:01:13.540
"I don't need another animal," said Fritz, who was in charge of Lightfoot the donkey, and Pounce the eagle.

14
00:01:13.541 --> 00:01:16.481
Meanwhile my wife and I had our own charges.

15
00:01:16.482 --> 00:01:22.854
The boys had elected her mistress of Grizzle, the donkey, while I was made supervisor of all the animals.

16
00:01:22.855 --> 00:01:25.965
That left Franz as caretaker of the bull.

17
00:01:25.966 --> 00:01:29.219
"I'll call him Grumble," he said happily.

18
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.456
"Because of that low grumbling sound he makes."

19
00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:38.361
For two months we worked on completing Rockburg, our new home in the cave.

20
00:01:38.362 --> 00:01:44.673
One morning just after we finished, I realized it was the anniversary of our escape from the wreck.

21
00:01:44.674 --> 00:01:48.904
Throughout the morning I pondered how we should mark this occasion.

22
00:01:48.905 --> 00:01:54.484
At lunch I announced that we would celebrate with a day of thanksgiving and athletic contests.

23
00:01:54.485 --> 00:01:57.389
"Will we run races?" asked Ernest.

24
00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.362
"Will there be prizes?" little Franz asked eagerly.

25
00:02:01.363 --> 00:02:06.499
"Yes, there will be prizes," I replied. "Mother and I will be the judges.

26
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.379
Now, trumpeters, announce the opening of the games!"

27
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:17.292
I clapped my hands loudly. Startled, our ducks and geese responded with loud quacks and honks.

28
00:02:17.293 --> 00:02:21.251
This amused the boys, who were eager to begin the competition.

29
00:02:21.252 --> 00:02:23.667
"Let's have shooting first," I said.

30
00:02:23.668 --> 00:02:27.518
I set up a target and the boys tried to hit the bull's-eye.

31
00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:31.987
After taking turns with a gun, they tried again with bow and arrow.

32
00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:36.665
Although Fritz was declared the winner, all my sons were very skilled.

33
00:02:36.666 --> 00:02:40.022
The next event was a race for the three older boys.

34
00:02:40.023 --> 00:02:45.358
"Run to Falconhurst," I said, "and retrieve the jackknife I accidentally left behind.

35
00:02:45.359 --> 00:02:48.090
It should be on the table near my bed.

36
00:02:48.091 --> 00:02:54.023
The first one back with the knife will be the winner. Ready, set, go!"

37
00:02:54.024 --> 00:02:58.747
Fritz and Jack took off at top speed while Ernest set a slow, steady pace.

38
00:02:58.748 --> 00:03:02.351
"I predict Ernest will win," said my wife.

39
00:03:02.352 --> 00:03:07.597
Long before we expected anyone back, we heard a tremendous galloping sound.

40
00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:11.934
Jack rode up on his buffalo with the two donkeys tearing after him.

41
00:03:11.935 --> 00:03:15.024
He shouted merrily as he dashed up to us.

42
00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:18.631
"You were supposed to race on your own two feet!" I said.

43
00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:22.938
"I didn't have a chance of winning, so I caught Storm and made him gallop back.

44
00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:25.376
Grizzle and Lightfoot decided to join me."

45
00:03:25.377 --> 00:03:29.946
After a while the other boys arrived. Ernest held up the jackknife.

46
00:03:29.947 --> 00:03:34.128
"I got to Falconhurst at least two minutes ahead of Fritz," he said.

47
00:03:34.129 --> 00:03:38.689
"Well done," I said. "And now it's time for climbing."

48
00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.431
In this contest Jack performed wonders.

49
00:03:41.432 --> 00:03:45.243
He ascended the highest palm trees with remarkable agility.

50
00:03:45.244 --> 00:03:49.742
Fritz and Ernest climbed well but couldn't equal the skill of their younger brother.

51
00:03:49.743 --> 00:03:52.974
Riding came next with Jack performing the best.

52
00:03:52.975 --> 00:03:57.423
I thought this event was over until little Franz appeared leading Grumble.

53
00:03:57.424 --> 00:04:00.567
The young bull was wearing a saddle and bridle.

54
00:04:00.568 --> 00:04:06.974
Franz saluted us. "Prepare to see something new and wonderful!"

55
00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:11.079
Holding the end of a long lead, he gave a series of commands.

56
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.331
Grumble proceeded to walk, trot, and gallop.

57
00:04:14.332 --> 00:04:18.259
Then Franz mounted the bull and rode awkwardly in a circle.

58
00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:23.681
The final contest was swimming, and Fritz showed himself to be a master of the sport.

59
00:04:23.682 --> 00:04:27.986
Meanwhile my wife had returned to Rockburg to prepare the prizes.

60
00:04:27.987 --> 00:04:31.709
I found her seated with the prizes laid out by her side.

61
00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.880
The boys marched in, pretending to play various instruments.

62
00:04:35.881 --> 00:04:39.410
They bowed before her as if she were a queen.

63
00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:44.267
"For skill in shooting and swimming . . ." She paused dramatically.

64
00:04:44.268 --> 00:04:48.598
"I give this rifle and hunting knife to Fritz."

65
00:04:48.599 --> 00:04:53.808
As the winner of the race to Falconhurst, Ernest received a handsome gold watch.

66
00:04:53.809 --> 00:05:00.647
Jack was awarded a pair of silver-plated spurs and a whip for his skill at climbing and riding.

67
00:05:00.648 --> 00:05:04.636
"And now a special prize," said my wife.

68
00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:11.357
"For extraordinary skill in bull-training, I present these stirrups to Franz."

69
00:05:11.358 --> 00:05:20.837
We closed the day by remembering everything that had happened a year ago and giving thanks for our new life.
